.TH SDL_CreatePopupWindow 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CreatePopupWindow \- Create a child popup window of the specified parent window.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Window * SDL_CreatePopupWindow(SDL_Window *parent, int offset_x, int offset_y, int w, int h, SDL_WindowFlags flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The window size is a request and may be different than expected based on the desktop layout and window manager policies\[char46] Your application should be prepared to handle a window of any size\[char46]
.PP
The flags parameter
.BR must
contain at least one of the following:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_TOOLTIP :
The popup window is a tooltip and will not pass any input events\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_POPUP_MENU :
The popup window is a popup menu\[char46] The topmost popup menu will implicitly gain the keyboard focus\[char46]
.PP
The following flags are not relevant to popup window creation and will be ignored:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_MINIMIZED
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_MAXIMIZED
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_BORDERLESS
.PP
The following flags are incompatible with popup window creation and will cause it to fail:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_UTILITY
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_MODAL
.PP
The parent parameter
.BR must
be non-null and a valid window\[char46] The parent of a popup window can be either a regular, toplevel window, or another popup window\[char46]
.PP
Popup windows cannot be minimized, maximized, made fullscreen, raised, flash, be made a modal window, be the parent of a toplevel window, or grab the mouse and/or keyboard\[char46] Attempts to do so will fail\[char46]
.PP
Popup windows implicitly do not have a border/decorations and do not appear on the taskbar/dock or in lists of windows such as alt-tab menus\[char46]
.PP
By default, popup window positions will automatically be constrained to keep the entire window within display bounds\[char46] This can be overridden with the
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_CONSTRAIN_POPUP_BOOLEAN
property\[char46]
.PP
By default, popup menus will automatically grab keyboard focus from the parent when shown\[char46] This behavior can be overridden by setting the
.BR SDL_WINDOW_NOT_FOCUSABLE
flag, setting the
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_FOCUSABLE_BOOLEAN
property to false, or toggling it after creation via the
.BR SDL_SetWindowFocusable()
function\[char46]
.PP
If a parent window is hidden or destroyed, any child popup windows will be recursively hidden or destroyed as well\[char46] Child popup windows not explicitly hidden will be restored when the parent is shown\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I parent
the parent of the window, must not be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I offset_x
the x position of the popup window relative to the origin of the parent\[char46]
.TP
.I offset_y
the y position of the popup window relative to the origin of the parent window\[char46]
.TP
.I w
the width of the window\[char46]
.TP
.I h
the height of the window\[char46]
.TP
.I flags

.BR SDL_WINDOW_TOOLTIP
or
.BR SDL_WINDOW_POPUP_MENU ,
and zero or more additional
.BR SDL_WindowFlags
OR\(aqd together\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the window that was created or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateWindow (3),
